# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules.
#
# WHY THIS FILE: `/_next/static/*` and repo artwork (smoke/brand/collections)
# are served DIRECTLY by the Cloudflare assets layer — requests never reach
# the Next.js worker, so the Cache-Control entries in next.config.ts
# headers() do NOT apply to them. Workers Assets reads this file instead
# (same syntax as Cloudflare Pages `_headers`).
#
# Without it every asset shipped `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`:
# browsers revalidated every chunk/CSS/font/image on EVERY page view
# (Pingdom "leverage browser caching" / "missing expire headers"), repeat
# loads re-downloaded ~1.6MB of content that had not changed.
#
# Order matters: later matching rules override earlier ones for the same
# header key. The most specific (immutable) rules come last.
# ============================================================================

# --- Default for asset-served files: short fresh window + long SWR tail. ---
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# --- Next.js build output — content-hashed filenames, immutable. -----------
# Never changes under a URL, so cache for a year in browsers AND skip
# revalidation entirely (Pingdom's biggest repeat-visit win).
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
